1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,471
An island just grew by about 125 acres.

2
00:00:03,983 --> 00:00:09,324
On October 27, Japan's weather agency reported an underwater eruption,

3
00:00:09,324 --> 00:00:10,697
just off Iwo Jima.

4
00:00:11,183 --> 00:00:14,646
NASA's Landsat 9 caught the before and after.

5
00:00:14,646 --> 00:00:16,877
October 26, then November 11.

6
00:00:17,383 --> 00:00:20,537
Ash and rock piled up along the southeast beach.

7
00:00:20,537 --> 00:00:24,413
On November 16, Japan's Coast Guard confirmed the new land.

8
00:00:24,713 --> 00:00:26,786
Like and subscribe for more Earth news.

9
00:00:27,283 --> 00:00:29,083
That's about ninety football fields.

10
00:00:29,583 --> 00:00:30,620
Still unknown:

11
00:00:30,620 --> 00:00:31,953
how long it lasts.

12
00:00:31,953 --> 00:00:35,952
In 2023, waves washed new land here away within weeks.

13
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:40,697
NASA's Daniel Slayback expects this land to wash away within months too.

14
00:00:40,697 --> 00:00:43,116
But, he says, we'll have to wait and see.

15
00:00:43,617 --> 00:00:46,283
Now, what if every volcano erupted at once?

16
00:00:46,283 --> 00:00:47,896
Full story on the channel.
